<title>TURKEY: Turkey raises petroleum prices by 7-9 percent.</title>
<headline>Turkey raises petroleum prices by 7-9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey has raised petroleum prices by seven to nine percent, the second hike since the three-party coalition government took office in late June, state refinery Tupras said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the prices were raised &quot;because of rises in depreciation of the Turkish curreny against foreign currencies and changes of prices in international petroleum markets.&quot;</p>
<p>It said diesel and LPG prices were raised by seven percent, and super grade gasoline and fuel oil by nine percent.</p>
</text>
